From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dann2333 <dann2333@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: initialize edp_panel to NULL in trilin_dp_probe

trilin_dp_probe() declares `struct drm_panel *edp_panel;` without an
initializer.  It is only assigned inside the `if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(
fwnode_edp_panel))` branch, but `dp->edp_panel = edp_panel;` runs
unconditionally afterwards.

On Orion O6 the kernel boots via ACPI (UEFI loads no DTB), and the ACPI
tables do not expose an "edp-panel" device property.
fwnode_find_reference() therefore returns -ENOENT, the if-branch is
skipped, and `dp->edp_panel` is set to whatever uninitialized stack
slot held — typically string-shaped data left over from an earlier
function frame (e.g. 0xffff0a600031303a).

Later in trilin_dp_host_init() the test `if (dp->edp_panel)` passes
because the value is non-zero, drm_panel_prepare() is called with the
garbage pointer, and dev_warn(panel->dev, ...) inside drm_panel_prepare
faults on a level-2 translation, panicking the kernel.

The crash is timing-dependent because the stack slot's content varies
with KASLR seed and module load order.  Builds with CoreSight enabled
hit the bad value reliably; builds without it usually got a value that
happened to be zero or unmapped, masking the bug.

Initialize edp_panel to NULL at declaration so the unconditional
assignment is safe and the existing `if (dp->edp_panel)` guards behave
as intended on platforms (ACPI or DT) that do not provide an eDP panel.

This is a strict bug fix: no struct layout, ABI, or behavior change for
boards that DO have an edp-panel reference.  Out-of-tree display
modules are unaffected — their visible state of dp->edp_panel was
always meant to be NULL when no panel is wired up.

---
 src/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c b/src/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
--- a/src/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
+++ b/src/drivers/gpu/drm/cix/dptx/trilin_dptx.c
@@ -3252,7 +3252,7 @@ int trilin_dp_probe(struct trilin_dpsub *dpsub, struct drm_device *drm)
 	struct resource *res_dp, *res_phy, *res_rcsu = NULL;
 	struct device *dev;
 	struct fwnode_handle *fwnode_edp_panel;
-	struct drm_panel *edp_panel;
+	struct drm_panel *edp_panel = NULL;
 	int ret;
 	const char *str_prop;
 	u32 is_insmod = 0;
--
2.47.1
